@@ -3,8 +3,9 @@
 `docs/decisions.md` turns the 2026-11-06 direction into decided rules: accepted safe code has no
 implicit trap; every operation that could fail carries checked evidence (a decidable octagon checker
 proved sound in Lean, contracts with closed evidence, Lean theorems; no SMT) or a written failure
-branch. Termination is known before a program runs: proved, or permitted explicitly at its source
-loop, recursive cycle or boundary, never silently unknown. Per-function execution facts (termination,
+branch. Every function has termination evidence with its premises, or a report naming the
+explicitly permitted unresolved obligations, each permitted at its source loop, recursive cycle or
+boundary, never silently unknown. Per-function execution facts (termination,
 recursion depth, stack, abort, allocation, blocking, foreign calls) are reported, `bounded` is
 derived, and module or project policies may require them. The revised rows carry revision notes;
 `PHILOSOPHY.md` rules 16 and 18, `README.md` and R-0574 follow. Three spellings stay with the owner.
diff --git a/changelog.d/2026-11-08-bot-snapshot-files.md b/changelog.d/2026-11-08-bot-snapshot-files.md
deleted file mode 100644
index f8868112e..000000000
--- a/changelog.d/2026-11-08-bot-snapshot-files.md
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,7 +0,0 @@
-### The bot's launcher rebuilds a cached snapshot missing any file (2026-11-08)
-
-The launcher `scripts/land/install-bot.sh` writes judged a cached snapshot complete when each listed
-`SNAPSHOT` path existed, so a cache that had `scripts/land/` but lacked `scripts/land/bot.sh` was
-kept and failed on every run (Kimi, review of the slice-0 branch). It now requires every file the
-commit has under those paths (`git ls-tree`), and rebuilds otherwise. `scripts/checks/landing_bot.sh`
-runs the launcher's own cache step on a missing, an incomplete and a complete cache.
diff --git a/changelog.d/2026-11-08-gate-host-login.md b/changelog.d/2026-11-08-gate-host-login.md
deleted file mode 100644
index 154b2f1e8..000000000
--- a/changelog.d/2026-11-08-gate-host-login.md
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,10 +0,0 @@
-### The gate host checks its login before it fetches (2026-11-08)
-
-A landing check run from an account whose `concrete-ci-2` ssh alias is the root admin login
-(by design: the provisioned gate identity is `agent` on fede-256gb, which logs into `dev` with the
-`ci_gates` key, dotfiles `servers/agent-home.sh`) looked for `/root/concrete2` and reported only that
-the fetch failed. `scripts/land/gates_transport_ssh.sh` now checks the login on the host before
-anything is fetched: a root login is refused (gates never run as root), a login `id` cannot read is
-refused rather than taken as non-root, and a login without its gate clone names the account and
-path. Each is INCOMPLETE, never a pass. `scripts/checks/landing_script.sh` covers all three through
-the real transport, and none fetches.
diff --git a/changelog.d/2026-11-08-record-foundation.md b/changelog.d/2026-11-08-record-foundation.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..3851c5b1b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog.d/2026-11-08-record-foundation.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+### Owner decisions: the Lean foundation first, contracts C1–C10 (2026-11-07, 2026-11-08)
+
+- `docs/decisions.md` records the owner's answers verbatim. "ok to option b then for freeze the
+  foundation>?" (2026-11-07): the shared foundation is written and frozen in the Lean spec before
+  slice 1 builds on it, and each later slice adds its rules on top without rewriting it; this
+  answers the spec plan's scheduling question S1. "ok all recommended" (2026-11-08): every question
+  of the foundation proposal takes its recommendation, with the revisions of Q3.7, Q3.9, Q3.10 and
+  OD126 (target profiles), Q1.7 (release-context erasure only with a proof) and Q7.1, Q7.10 and
+  Q9.7 (lawful extensible registries) noted at each row, byte columns at the trap line and
+  `Secret<T>`'s layout at the information-flow row.
+- The approved proposal is `docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md`, the plan for the spec work from PLAN
+  step 3 on; the Lean spec stays the only home of the rules.
+- `ROADMAP.md` gains R-0607 to R-0616, one per contract, each with its home in the spec and its
+  gate; A2i and the freeze (R-0567) include them.
+- `docs/proposals/SPEC_UNIFICATION.md`, the spec's step plan, is reordered for the foundation: steps
+  3–19 write C1–C10 in dependency order on top of `Ident` and `Rules` (target and types, scalars,
+  layout and values, primitive contracts, syntax and front end, admission; then observations, the
+  hybrid store, the step relation, the evaluator, borrows, brands and authority, leakage, frames and
+  evidence with erasure), with every old feature fragment ported there; steps 20–23 close and
+  freeze the foundation; the slices follow on top of it from step 24.
+
+### Owner decisions: eleven plan and process decisions (2026-11-08)
+
+- "ok go ahead with all the decisions": UBSan leaves the slice-0 gates (it checks nothing on LLVM IR
+  input; ASan stays); the BIR → LCB-IR adapter theorem is complete (an error produces no artifact,
+  success implies correctness); the landing scripts shrink (R-0617); Claude's quota goes to the
+  critical path; the lexer starts now against the spec's Lexical rules (R-0620); only its LL(1)
+  parser waits for the approved written grammar (R-0622); one writer for `docs/decisions.md`
+  and `ROADMAP.md`; review rounds are capped by risk, 2, 3 and 5 (R-0618); one clones folder
+  (R-0619); a no-libc runtime around slices 24–25 (R-0621); a report-only compile-speed budget
+  (R-0550); and the ISS-0014 F7 termination wording, applied in `docs/decisions.md`, `README.md`,
+  `docs/PHILOSOPHY.md` and the no-hidden-traps changelog fragment (ISS-0014 closed). The process rules are in `AGENTS.md`.
+
+### Owner decisions: agy reviews, the std-per-slice table, the written grammar and a speed target (2026-11-08)
+
+- "also remember we have agy not only codex kimi and claude": every branch gets an agy review beside
+  Codex and Kimi (AGENTS.md, the review row).
+- "ok let's do 2, for now let's not do 3": `ROADMAP.md` gains the std-per-slice table (each module's
+  slice, spec home, std source, evidence due and the showcases that need it, with the stages that
+  need a module before it arrives flagged for the owner); a user-guide chapter per slice is not done
+  for now.
+- "ok do the written grammar": the full surface grammar is written down for the owner's review
+  before the parser, then encoded in Lean as the grammar judgment (R-0622); only R-0620's parser
+  waits for it. The lexer starts now against the spec's Lexical rules.
+- "and yes speed target is fine": speed and size stay report-only until grep at slice 16, when the
+  owner sets a target against C from measured data (R-0623).
+- Recorded the owner's confirmation that capabilities stay as decided, `with(...)` permission sets
+  plus grant values, with no revision; foundation contract C5 is written to the decided authority
+  rules. Added R-0624: whether destroying a collection needs `with(Alloc)` when its release
+  metadata travels with it, decided with slice 19.
diff --git a/changelog.d/2026-11-08-review-blockers.md b/changelog.d/2026-11-08-review-blockers.md
deleted file mode 100644
index 1d8cc6e8a..000000000
--- a/changelog.d/2026-11-08-review-blockers.md
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,14 +0,0 @@
-### Two landing-tool gaps a train review found (2026-11-08)
-
-The review of train/slice0 (9ebdda15b2) reported two defects in code already on main.
-`scripts/checks/sandbox_isolation.sh` scanned only `scripts/*.sh` and `scripts/*/*.sh`, so a
-repository-making script two directories down, or one without a `.sh` suffix, was never checked.
-The scan now covers every shell script under `scripts/` at any depth (a `*.sh` file or an sh/bash
-shebang), and a control plants an unsandboxed maker three directories down and a suffixless one,
-both refused, and a sandboxed one at depth, accepted.
-`scripts/land/install-bot.sh`'s launcher snapshotted only `scripts/land` and `git_sandbox.sh`, so
-`train.sh`'s review provenance found no `scripts/review/verify.sh` and refused every train run by
-the bot. The snapshot is now one `SNAPSHOT` list covering every file the landing scripts read
-outside `scripts/land` (`verify.sh`, `prepush_record.sh` and the `treestate.sh` it sources); an
-incomplete cached snapshot is rebuilt; `scripts/checks/landing_bot.sh` fails when a landing script
-reads a path the list lacks, with the pre-fix list as its control.
